IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bkv-law`

-- Seat layer: a person who asks a federal authority for a document about the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases.
-- It asks that person's questions, takes plain facts as inputs, builds the law layer's record internally and calls the law layer's rules.
-- It restates no rule. Target compiler: main.
-- The article's footnote 8 assumes the statement was independently prepared and submitted as non-confidential and contains no internal deliberations,
-- personal data, trade secrets or copyright-protected material: here those assumptions are the input `another ground applies` being false.

GIVEN
    `federal request`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `prepared outside`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `submitted to the Council` IS A BOOLEAN
    `recommendation or report` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another ground applies`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `another duty attaches`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Request for a document`
`the request that` `federal request` `prepared outside` `submitted to the Council` `recommendation or report` `another ground applies` `another duty attaches` MEANS
    `Request for a document` WITH
        `is addressed to a federal authority and asks for official information` IS `federal request`
        `the document was prepared outside the Council and the Ministry` IS `prepared outside`
        `the document was submitted to the Council for its deliberations` IS `submitted to the Council`
        `the document is a recommendation an opinion or a closing report of the Council` IS `recommendation or report`
        `another ground for refusing access applies` IS `another ground applies`
        `another statutory confidentiality duty attaches to the document` IS `another duty attaches`

§ `Can I get the document under the Freedom of Information Act?`

@export Am I entitled to access to this document of the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases under the Freedom of Information Act, reading § 9(5) BKV as it has stood since 1 August 2026? Answers yes or no, from § 1(1) and § 3 no. 4 IFG.
GIVEN
    `federal request`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you ask a federal authority, such as the Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, for official information.
    `prepared outside`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was prepared outside the Expert Advisory Council and the Ministry, for example a statement written by an association; false if it was made inside.
    `submitted to the Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was submitted to the Expert Advisory Council for its deliberations.
    `recommendation or report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document is a recommendation, an opinion or a closing report of the Council, the documents § 9(5) sentence 1 BKV makes public.
    `another ground applies`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if another ground for refusing access applies, such as personal data, a trade secret, copyright or the authority's internal deliberations; false if none does.
    `another duty attaches`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a statutory confidentiality duty other than § 9(5) BKV attaches to the document, for example the members' duty of confidentiality; false if none does.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I entitled to access with section 9(5) BKV as in force` MEANS
    `the requester is entitled to access under the reading` `as in force from 1 August 2026` (`the request that` `federal request` `prepared outside` `submitted to the Council` `recommendation or report` `another ground applies` `another duty attaches`)

-- The next group only arises if the document is an external paper submitted to the Council, the kind the 2026 amendment brought under § 9(5).
-- A form can ask "Was it written outside the Council?" before showing it.
§ `What if the 2026 amendment of § 9(5) BKV is void?`

@export Am I entitled to access to this document of the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases under the Freedom of Information Act, if the 2026 amendment of § 9(5) BKV is void because the amending regulation did not cite § 9(1a) sentence 4 of Book VII of the Social Code? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    `federal request`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you ask a federal authority, such as the Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, for official information.
    `prepared outside`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was prepared outside the Expert Advisory Council and the Ministry, for example a statement written by an association; false if it was made inside.
    `submitted to the Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was submitted to the Expert Advisory Council for its deliberations.
    `recommendation or report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document is a recommendation, an opinion or a closing report of the Council, the documents § 9(5) sentence 1 BKV makes public.
    `another ground applies`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if another ground for refusing access applies, such as personal data, a trade secret, copyright or the authority's internal deliberations; false if none does.
    `another duty attaches`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a statutory confidentiality duty other than § 9(5) BKV attaches to the document, for example the members' duty of confidentiality; false if none does.
    `an exception applies`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2026 amendment of § 9(5) BKV stands: false assumes none applies and the amendment is void.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I entitled to access if the 2026 amendment is void` MEANS
    `the requester is entitled to access under the reading` (`the reading of section 9(5) BKV to apply` `an exception applies`) (`the request that` `federal request` `prepared outside` `submitted to the Council` `recommendation or report` `another ground applies` `another duty attaches`)

§ `Does § 9(5) BKV make the document confidential?`

@export Does § 9(5) BKV, as in force since 1 August 2026, make this paper of the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases confidential? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    `federal request`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you ask a federal authority, such as the Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, for official information.
    `prepared outside`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was prepared outside the Expert Advisory Council and the Ministry, for example a statement written by an association; false if it was made inside.
    `submitted to the Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was submitted to the Expert Advisory Council for its deliberations.
    `recommendation or report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document is a recommendation, an opinion or a closing report of the Council, the documents § 9(5) sentence 1 BKV makes public.
    `another ground applies`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if another ground for refusing access applies, such as personal data, a trade secret, copyright or the authority's internal deliberations; false if none does.
    `another duty attaches`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a statutory confidentiality duty other than § 9(5) BKV attaches to the document, for example the members' duty of confidentiality; false if none does.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is the document confidential under section 9(5) BKV as in force` MEANS
    `section 9(5) BKV makes the document confidential under the reading` `as in force from 1 August 2026` (`the request that` `federal request` `prepared outside` `submitted to the Council` `recommendation or report` `another ground applies` `another duty attaches`)

@export Does § 9(5) BKV make this paper of the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases confidential, if the 2026 amendment is void and the earlier wording, which covered only papers made inside, applies? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    `federal request`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you ask a federal authority, such as the Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, for official information.
    `prepared outside`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was prepared outside the Expert Advisory Council and the Ministry, for example a statement written by an association; false if it was made inside.
    `submitted to the Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was submitted to the Expert Advisory Council for its deliberations.
    `recommendation or report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document is a recommendation, an opinion or a closing report of the Council, the documents § 9(5) sentence 1 BKV makes public.
    `another ground applies`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if another ground for refusing access applies, such as personal data, a trade secret, copyright or the authority's internal deliberations; false if none does.
    `another duty attaches`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a statutory confidentiality duty other than § 9(5) BKV attaches to the document, for example the members' duty of confidentiality; false if none does.
    `an exception applies`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2026 amendment of § 9(5) BKV stands: false assumes none applies and the amendment is void.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is the document confidential if the 2026 amendment is void` MEANS
    `section 9(5) BKV makes the document confidential under the reading` (`the reading of section 9(5) BKV to apply` `an exception applies`) (`the request that` `federal request` `prepared outside` `submitted to the Council` `recommendation or report` `another ground applies` `another duty attaches`)

§ `Did the 2026 amending regulation cite the power for the confidentiality rule?`

@export Does the preamble of the Seventh Regulation amending the Occupational Diseases Regulation (Federal Law Gazette 2026 I Nr. 210) cite § 9(1a) sentence 4 of Book VII of the Social Code, the power to settle the details of the Council's status and organisation? Answers yes or no, from the gazette text of the preamble.
`does the 2026 preamble cite the power for the confidentiality rule` MEANS
    `the preamble cites the power`
        `the power needed to make the confidentiality rule`
        `the powers cited in the preamble of the Seventh Amending Regulation`
